hadiths[18]{hadithnumber,text}:
"884","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him): We set out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the year of Hudaybiyyah. The companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hastily put on ihram, but I had not yet put on ihram. Then we were informed that there was an enemy at the place of Ghaiqah who wanted to fight. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proceeded, and I (Abu Qatadah) was also with his companions. Then my companions saw a wild donkey (onager), and they began to look at each other and laugh (I realized they were laughing at the sight of game). Then I also looked up and saw the wild donkey. I chased it on my horse and shot it with an arrow, bringing it down. Then I asked those people for help, but they refused to help me (so I slaughtered it myself). Then we all ate its meat. After that, I rode my horse at full speed to search for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). We became afraid that we might be separated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then (on the way) I met a man from Banu Ghifar. I asked him, ""Where did you leave the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)?"" He said, ""I left the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the spring called Ta‘hn, and his intention was to rest at the place of Suqya."" (After asking this, I set off) and joined the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When I reached him, I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! The companions have sent me; they send you peace and Allah's mercy, and they fear that the enemy may separate them from you, so please wait for them."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did so. Then I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! We hunted a wild donkey, and we have some of its meat left."" So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his companions, ""Eat."" Even though they were all in ihram."
"885","Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates in one narration that we were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the place of Qahah, three miles from Madinah, and some of us were in the state of Ihram and some were not in Ihram. Then the entire hadith was narrated. See the chapter: If a person not in Ihram hunts and gives it as a gift to a person in Ihram, then it is permissible for the person in Ihram to eat it... (the hadith was narrated)."
"886","It is narrated in another narration from Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) that when he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he (peace be upon him) asked the companions (may Allah be pleased with them): ""Did any of you tell Abu Qatadah to attack that game?"" They replied, ""No."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Then there is no harm, eat the remaining meat of it."""
"887","Narrated from Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that Sa'b bin Jaththamah Al-Laithi (may Allah be pleased with him) presented a wild donkey as a gift to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) while he (peace be upon him) was at the place of Abwa or the place of Waddan, so he (peace be upon him) returned it. Then, when he saw the sadness on his face, he (peace be upon him) said: ""We have only returned it because we are in the state of Ihram."""
"888","Narrated from Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There are five harmful animals that may be killed even in the state of Ihram: the crow, the kite, the scorpion, the mouse, and the biting dog."""
"889","Narrated Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him): While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a cave at Mina, Surah Al-Mursalat was revealed to him. He began to recite it, and I started memorizing it from him as he recited. While he was still reciting it, suddenly a snake leapt towards us. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Kill it."" So we rushed towards it, but it escaped. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) then said: ""It has been saved from your harm just as you have been saved from its harm."""
"890","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said about the lizard: ""It is harmful."" But I did not hear him (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) giving the order to kill it. (However, it should be killed.)"
"891","Narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day Makkah was conquered: ""There is no migration left now, but jihad and intention (their reward remains). So whenever you are called for jihad, then (immediately) set out."""
"892","`Sayyiduna Ibn Buhaina (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that` the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had cupping done in the middle of his head at the place of Lahy Jamal while he was in the state of Ihram."
"893","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Umm al-Mu'mineen Maymunah (may Allah be pleased with her) while he was in the state of Ihram."
"894","It was asked from Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wash his blessed head while in the state of Ihram. So Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub (may Allah be pleased with him), who was taking a bath behind a cloth screen (the narrator says), placed his hand on the cloth and lowered it until I began to see his head. Then he said to a person, ""Pour water,"" so that person poured water on his head. Then he moved his head with both his hands, to the front and to the back. After that, he said, ""I saw the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) doing exactly like this."""
"895","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah in the year of the conquest of Makkah, there was a helmet on his blessed head. When he (peace be upon him) removed it, a man came to him and said: ""The wretched disbeliever named Ibn Khatal is clinging to the curtains of the Ka'bah."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Kill him there."""
"896","Narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that a woman from the tribe of Juhaina came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: ""My mother had vowed to perform Hajj but she could not perform it before she died. So, should I perform Hajj on her behalf?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Yes, perform Hajj on her behalf. Tell me, if your mother had a debt, would you not pay it off for her? So, fulfill Allah's debt, for Allah has more right that His debt be fulfilled."""
"897","Sayedna Saib bin Yazid (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I was made to perform Hajj with the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) and I was seven years old."
"898","Narrated Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from his Hajj, he said to Umm Sinan Ansariyyah: ""What prevented you from performing Hajj?"" She replied, ""So-and-so"" (referring to her husband) ""had two camels for carrying water; he went for Hajj on one, and the other is used to irrigate our land."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Well, then perform Umrah, for indeed performing Umrah in Ramadan is equivalent to performing Hajj with me."""
"899","`Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him)`, who participated in twelve battles with the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), used to say that I heard four things from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), which I found good and pleasing (these are the things): ""No woman should travel for two days without her husband or a mahram, and one should not fast on two days, i.e., Eid al-Fitr and Eid al-Adha, and after two prayers, i.e., after the Asr prayer until sunset and after the Fajr prayer until sunrise, no prayer should be performed, and one should not undertake a journey except towards three mosques: Masjid al-Haram (i.e., the Ka'bah), my mosque (i.e., Masjid Nabawi), and Masjid al-Aqsa (i.e., Bayt al-Maqdis)."""
"900","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) saw an old man being led between his two sons. The Prophet (peace be upon him) asked: ""What has happened to him?"" The people replied that he had vowed to go on foot. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Allah is not in need of him punishing himself."" And he ordered the old man to ride."
"901","Narrated by Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Amir (may Allah be pleased with him): My sister vowed to walk to the House of Allah (the Ka'bah), and she asked me to inquire about this from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: ""She should walk a little and also ride."""
